{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480928-legacies-and-and-final-attainments","id":1480928,"title":"Legacies and And Final Attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-12T22:09:38-07:00","id":1480928,"title":"Legacies and And Final Attainments","content":"Hi guys. So,I was fishing through Dev comments on legacies,and I latched on the idea of the Final Attainments<br /> First let's see their relation to Ascension<br /> <br /> From Imperial Mysteries<br /> <br /> Final Attainment<br /> Various Legacies speak of a fourth and Final Attainment. <br /> A mage who attains it becomes an Epitome of her Legacy. <br /> More often than not, even the Legacy\u2019s founder fails to <br /> manifest the fourth Attainment but according to some <br /> sorcerers, discovering it makes Ascension possible. <br /> Ascension through the Final Attainment is a notable <br /> path in that it apparently doesn\u2019t require archmastery. If it <br /> follows the patterns Legacies use, it should be available to <br /> Masters \u2014 but not all Masters.<br /> Legacy scholars possess a rough understanding of the theo-<br /> retical prerequisites, which in game terms would be a Gnosis <br /> of 9 and fi ve dots in the Legacy\u2019s primary Arcanum. They <br /> disagree as to whether the Final Attainment is common to <br /> the Legacy or unique to the individual, but most believe that <br /> Gnosis and magical ability alone won\u2019t grant it. One further <br /> achievement is necessary. Again, the fi nal requirement may be <br /> universal or personal. Perfected Adepts whisper that a warrior <br /> called the Dragon Manifest hunts anyone searching for its <br /> Final Attainment, and Walkers in Mist speak of defeating a <br /> living darkness deep within their Mists.<br /> Legends say that the Final Attainment alone does not <br /> guarantee Ascension, but makes it possible. The Epitome <br /> undertakes a quest to prove herself the living archetype <br /> of her Legacy. Only then may she unite with its Supernal <br /> principle.<br /> <br /> From comments by Dave Brookshaw, the first mage 2e Dev.<br /> He answered the question by Raibran<br /> Raibran<br /> In 1e, Legacies had in addition to their three attainments a legendary \u201cfourth attainment\u201d, usually implied to go along with Archmastery. Do 2e Legacies have a \u201csixth attainment\u201d, or is that whole concept scrapped?<br /> <br /> Also, Mysterium! Magic Indiana Jones!<br /> <br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw<br /> September 3, 2014 at 5:07 pm<br /> The Fourth (now Fifth) was Gnosis 9 or 10, and duplicated a master-level spell. Attaining it makes you an \u201cExemplar,\u201d but it\u2019s rare to find anyone using the title.<br /> <br /> The *Final* Attainment is something that legendarily happens to some Exemplars \u2013 they get caught up in a Mystery Play to do with reaching the peak of their Legacy, and some Ascend at the end of it.<br /> <br /> Archmastery is not required to be an Exemplar. Just patience and success as a mage.<br /> <br /> I thought it'd be fun if we could get together to talk about what do you think the Final Attainment would be for your favourie legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-13-2022, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:45:05-07:00","id":1481085,"title":"","content":"I always pictured the final attainment simply having some common elements within a legacy but with it being unique to the member.<br /> <br /> One Tamer of Fire might make sweeping and glorious speeches that inspire armies (cities? nations?) while another might be able to penetrate the Lie when discussing one on one. One Dreamspeaker might be able to project into astral, spirit, and physical simultaneously, while another might become able to withstand the ravages of the Ecstatic Winds, and yet another might be able to start redefining the physical world as a Dreamer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T10:55:50-07:00","id":1481095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1480928-legacies-and-and-final-attainments?p=1481085#post1481085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always pictured the final attainment simply having some common elements within a legacy but with it being unique to the member.<br /> <br /> One Tamer of Fire might make sweeping and glorious speeches that inspire armies (cities? nations?) while another might be able to penetrate the Lie when discussing one on one. One Dreamspeaker might be able to project into astral, spirit, and physical simultaneously, while another might become able to withstand the ravages of the Ecstatic Winds, and yet another might be able to start redefining the physical world as a Dreamer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what I'm thinking too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T12:17:29-07:00","id":1481104,"title":"","content":"I remember that the Thrice Great believe that obtaining the final Attainment requires them to use a ritual to call across the Abyss to the Oracle that supposedly founded their Legacy. I imagine a final Attainment would allow them to create a ritual site that allows them to easily summon any beings resonant with the planetary correspondents (Fallen spirits, Supernal summons, etc) and allow any Essence resonant with the spell to be treated as Pneuma while within its confines. The idea is that while creating a new Celestial Ladder is the purview of archmasters, an Exemplar of this Legacy is fully aware of the workings of the Planetary Ladder and can use hermetic ritual to harness its infrastructure to bring some of the power of the Supernal to the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:24:48-07:00","id":1481125,"title":"","content":"I really like rhat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}